1332 0 obj
  << /ActualText (1\056 Students Are Our Focus\050\nWe are a multi\055disciplined human\055centered design team that applies the user\055centered approach to our curriculum to train human\055centered designers\056 The students are your users\056 You\054 as the instructor\054 are our \050the curriculum team\031s\051 user\056 All user experience \050UX\051\057user interface \050UI\051 course materials are established on this foundation so that the instructional team can extend their user\055first approach throughout the 24 weeks of this program and beyond\056\nStudents are our focus\056 This applies to every aspect of the UX\057UI Boot Camp\024from the instructional staff to student support managers\054 to career services\054 and beyond\056 Our No Back Row\256 philosophy \050\043nobackrow\051 offers a program for students to reach their highest learning potential\056\n)
     /K [ 2 ]
     /P 1333 0 R
     /Pg 1328 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1333 0 obj
  << /K [ 1332 0 R ]
     /P 1366 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 1328 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1334 0 obj
  << /ActualText (2\056 The Design Process Is the Best Design Tool\050\nOur students have a wide range of skills coming into the UX\057UI Boot Camp\056 Some come from a design background while others might be from the medical field\056 If students gain experience with the design process\054 they will be more productive and workplace\055ready for the new roles they will fill\056 The design software world changes quickly\054 which is why executing the design process is more important than understanding any one design tool\056 UX\057UI Boot Camp is about design as a process and not so much about which tool you use to apply that knowledge\056 Many different tools are used to execute the design process\054 and we will lean heavily on pen and paper first\054 graduating to software like Figma\054 Adobe XD\054 and InVision to execute digital prototyping\056 Design software is not a one\055way street\054 and if students want to use Sketch or other tools to execute their prototyping process\054 they may\056\n    By teaching students the process\054 we\031re empowering them to focus on more valuable skills\056 Give a person a tool\054 and they can use it in a specific context\056 Teach a person why a tool is needed and how it is relevant to the overall process\054 and they will solve problems and create great things\056\n)
     /K [ 3 ]
     /P 1335 0 R
     /Pg 1328 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1335 0 obj
  << /K [ 1334 0 R ]
     /P 1366 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 1328 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1336 0 obj
  << /ActualText (3\056 Struggle Gives Rise to Real Learning\050\nThe boot camp learning environment is challenging by design\056 Learning research tells us that an unchallenged brain doesn\031t learn\054 so if students never struggle\054 they won\031t benefit from the course\056 Our curriculum is built to be supportive but tough so that students\047 minds are challenged\054 and they learn\056 We also cover a wide range of skills from UX to UI to front\055end development\056 Being an expert at everything in a six\055month boot camp is an unreasonable expectation\056 However\054 the curriculum is designed to put students on the right path and to encourage them to keep learning\054 even when it is hard\056\n\n)
     /K [ 4 ]
     /P 1337 0 R
     /Pg 1328 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

