1346 0 obj
  << /ActualText (4\056 Hands\055on Practice Through Prototyping\050\nThrough the design thinking process\054 students are getting hands\055on practice with activities using tangible materials \050sticky notes\054 paper\054 whiteboards\054 etc\056\051 and digital executions \050Adobe XD\054 InVision\054 Slack\054 etc\056\051\056 The curriculum also applies Designerly Ways of Knowing \050DWOK\051 principles\056\nThe following are highlights from Grounding IS Design Education in the First Principles of a Designerly Way of Knowing\072  Design is continuous\056 Exploring and learning to happen in a dynamic social environment \050classroom\051 and through interactive technology\056 Design reconciles worldviews\056 Uses empathy to create human\055centered solutions\056 The medium of construction \050the web\051 determines the design choices \050size\054 UI elements\054 etc\056\051\056 Prototyping UIs designed in context to the technology and the user\031s needs\056 Humans\031 knowledge and conscious expression are imperfect\056 Failure is essential for validating a solution\056 User testing will help create tighter iterative cycles\056 The operative appreciative systems determine the whole of the design space\056 Stakeholders and designers apply a perception of the world through a worldview that determines what cues they notice to determine their sense of approval or displeasure\056 Designers must build bridges to attain cohesion between the stakeholder\031s needs and the user\031s needs\056\n\n\n)
     /K [ 9 ]
     /P 1347 0 R
     /Pg 1328 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1347 0 obj
  << /K [ 1346 0 R ]
     /P 1366 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 1328 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1348 0 obj
  << /ActualText (Chris R\056 Becker     \174    Product Design Portfolio    \174   2021)
     /K [ 10 ]
     /P 1349 0 R
     /Pg 1328 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1349 0 obj
  << /K [ 1348 0 R ]
     /P 1366 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 1328 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1350 0 obj
  << /ActualText (5\056 Learning Through Backward Design\050\nWe have developed the UX\057UI curriculum through a backward design methodology\056 We begin with the learning objectives of a unit and define what students are expected to learn and be able to do for their week\031s assignment\056 The lesson creation proceeds \034backward\035 to create lesson plans\054 activities\054 discussions\054 and reviews that achieve those skills throughout each class and each unit\056)
     /K [ 11 ]
     /P 1351 0 R
     /Pg 1328 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1351 0 obj
  << /K [ 1350 0 R ]
     /P 1366 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 1328 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1352 0 obj
  << /ActualText (6\056 UX\057UI Designers Should Be \034Code Conversational\035\n\050UX\057UI designers are not developers\054 and we do not expect them to be\056 However\054 the reality is that a UX\057UI designer\031s work ends up as code whether that be a software solution\054 a website\054 or any other user\055facing interface\056 Our students will be joining a fast\055moving profession that requires them to work alongside developers as teammates\056 Learning and being able to code some HTML\057CSS\057JavaScript will get them some experience working on human\055centered code problems together\056 This will\054 in turn\054 prepare them to join a team and work alongside their developer colleagues to execute solutions through software prototypes\056)
     /K [ 12 ]
     /P 1353 0 R
     /Pg 1328 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1353 0 obj
  << /K [ 1352 0 R ]
     /P 1366 0 R
     /S /P
     /Pg 1328 0 R
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

1354 0 obj
  << /ActualText (7\056 Case Study\023Driven UX\057UI Portfolios Are Key to Student Success\n\050The design process happens over time and is best communicated through a case study that tells a story of how a designer went from nothing to something\056 A UX\057UI designer\031s value resides in how they think\054 and how they think is demonstrated through the deliverables that make up the design process\056Out in the \034real world\054\035 UX\057UI designers must share their thinking\054 work skills\054 and UX\057UI samples through a visual portfolio that helps highlight strengths and types of problems they are good at solving\056 This is typically done online\056 We assist our students in executing their design portfolios while allowing them to practice the design process and communicate their solutions through a series of case studies\056 We also prepare them for interviews that will help them get into their next role in the workplace or their career\056)
     /K [ 13 ]
     /P 1355 0 R
     /Pg 1328 0 R
     /S /Span
     /Type /StructElem
  >>
endobj

